	Introduction, Preface

	This lame door was actually written because I thought it was
	so easy to write so why use one from another person on my board!?
	So I used most of my energy on the design and I hope you like it :)

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	What will SysComment do for you?

	It will simple let your users choose who they wan't to give the
	comment then they've choosed the 'C' command inside /X!

	New feature in the 2.01 version is that you could give it fast
	commands like C 1 (for sysop) and C 2 (for cosysop). This idea
	comes from Fatal / Obscene, thanks :)

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	Instalation ..

	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/BBS.Cmd file:

	*C        Xm020Doors:SysCm

	For 3.x users.. Duplicate any bbscmd icon, change the path to
	the door in tooltypes and set it to an XIM Door.

	You could just put this door in any directory you like it
	doesn't matter, but you need the SysCm.CFG in the same directory!

	Now it's time to edit the SysCm.CFG file. Use any editor you like,
	Cygnus Ed for example. Just change the names and comments to
	your desired ones, it should be rather easy!

	REMEMBER everything is position dependent, that means that you
	         can't use more space than there is in the CFG file that
		 I sent with this package between the | | characters.

	Copy the AEDoor.library to your libs: directory! (if you don't
	already have it! :)

